+## Repository and workflow
+
+- This tree is generated: the outer taixin-halow-bridge repo stores `patches/*.patch` against the vendor commit `FW_BASE` (`scripts/upstream.env`), and `scripts/apply.sh` clones the vendor repo and applies them on a branch `bridge`. `web/` (the UI) lives only in the outer repo.
+- To change firmware: commit here on `bridge`, then run `scripts/export-patches.sh` in the outer repo (refuses to run with uncommitted changes; `project/txw4002a.mk` is ignored) and commit `patches/` together with any `web/` changes. Every patch's `[PATCH n/N]` line changes when the series grows; that is expected.
+- Branches: outer `main` ↔ firmware `bridge`. The online updater lives on outer `online-update` ↔ firmware `online-update` (one extra commit on top of `bridge`). To bring `main` changes over: rebase the firmware `online-update` onto `bridge` (regenerate `webui_page.h` on conflict), merge `main` into the outer `online-update` (no force push), rebuild `web/`, regenerate the page and re-export the patches.
+- Every change is built in CDK and boot-tested on hardware before it is committed.
+
 ## Conventions
 
-- Firmware sources use CRLF line endings. Keep them; in-place `sed -i` under Git Bash converts files to LF.
+- Files in this tree are stored with LF (`* text=auto eol=lf`), except `project/txw4002a.cdkproj` (CRLF upstream, applied with `--keep-cr`). The outer repo keeps `patches/*.patch` byte-exact (`-text`).
 - C style follows the vendor: `int32`/`uint8` types, `os_*` wrappers (`os_malloc`, `os_printf`, `os_strcmp`…), 4-space indent, `RET_OK`.
 - Comments in vendor files are partly Chinese; leave them as they are.
 - Check the dev-only `SYS_APP_*` flags (`project_config.h`) before shipping, along with demo credentials: default WiFi passphrase `12345678` and web password `admin`.
